 "literal": "Small bamboo fence, root-bearing jackfruit tree's / mountain slope lord! May you become of fitting nature! / Who are those who know that? Mountain slope / on a small branch a large fruit hanging, like that, this woman's / life is very small, but her love is indeed great!",
 "translation": "O lord of the mountain slopes, where small bamboo serves as a fence and jackfruit trees bear fruit right at their roots! May you act with fitting grace. Who is there to understand her state? Like a huge fruit hanging from a tiny branch on the mountain slope, her life is very small, but her love is immense.",
 "modern": "சிறிய மூங்கில்களை வேலியாகக் கொண்ட, வேரிலேயே பலாப்பழங்கள் காய்க்கும் மலைச்சரிவு நாட்டின் தலைவனே! நீ அவளை விரைந்து மணந்து கொள்ளும் நல்வாய்ப்பைப் பெறுவாயாக! அவளுடைய நிலையை யார்தான் அறிவார்கள்? மலைச்சரிவில் உள்ள ஒரு சிறிய கிளையிலே பெரிய பலாப்பழம் தொங்குவதைப் போல, இவளுடைய உயிர் மிகவும் சிறியது; ஆனால் இவள் உன்மேல் கொண்டுள்ள காதலோ மிகப் பெரியது.",
 "explanation": "The friend (தோழி) is speaking to the hero (தலைவன்) who has been coming secretly to meet the heroine (தலைவி). She urges him to marry her soon instead of continuing his secret visits. She compares the heroine's delicate life to a tiny branch holding a massive jackfruit. This imagery belongs to the Kuriñci (mountainous) landscape. The tiny branch represents the heroine's fragile life, while the heavy fruit represents her overwhelming love. If the hero delays marriage, her life might break under the weight of her love, just as the branch might snap under the weight of the fruit. Key words include 'சிறுகோடு' (small branch), 'பெரும்பழம்' (large fruit), 'உயிர்' (life), and 'காமம்' (love).",
